\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The voltage trace is one coordinate}
\date{2026-11-25}

\p{Let #{\varphi^{t}(x_{0})} be a [trajectory](fnip-0009). Its voltage
trace is the voltage coordinate of the point #{\varphi^{t}(x_{0})}.
In the Morris–Lecar pair of \ref{fnip-0005} that coordinate is #{V},
so the trace is the function #{t\mapsto V(t)}. The trajectory itself
is the pair #{(V(t),n(t))}.}

\p{At one fixed time, one value of #{V} belongs to many pairs. The
drawing of the pair is the phase portrait. The trace is the portrait
read along #{V}.}
